<title>UK: B.A.T firms on cigar reorganisation.</title>
<headline>B.A.T firms on cigar reorganisation.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in B.A.T Industries extended their gains after the UK conglomerate said it sold its Henri Wintermans Cigar Group and expects the sale to result in a small pre-tax profit.</p>
<p>At 1407 GMT, the shares were up 14-1/2p to 481.</p>
<p>The shares opened higher after a strong performance in Philip Morris shares overnight, dealers said.</p>
<p>Perceptions B.A.T shares were oversold also lent support, they said.</p>
<p>-- Debra Sherman, London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
</text>
